# modular-hx-ts — every environment variable, with its memory default.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) for local overrides. An EMPTY `.env` is a valid
# one: every default below runs the whole application with zero external
# dependencies. That is acceptance criterion 1, written as a file.
#
# Uncommenting the "rung 2" block at the bottom is the ENTIRE switch from
# memory to real infrastructure — a config change, never a code path.
#
# Each component declares its own configuration schema and all problems are
# reported at once (../ARCHITECTURE.md §8), so this file grows one block per
# module and every variable names the module that reads it. A variable no
# module reads does not belong here.

# ── Process ──────────────────────────────────────────────── L5 root ──
NODE_ENV=development
HOST=127.0.0.1

# ../PORTS.md offset +10 (APP_PORT) for this repo's 15420 base. Namespaced even
# for `make dev`, so two blueprints' dev servers do not fight over 8080.
PORT=15430

# How long lifecycle waits for components to stop before giving up. Must exceed
# the longest request timeout, or shutdown kills work that was about to finish.
SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# ── Logging ──────────────────────────────────────────── L1 `logger` ──
LOG_LEVEL=info
# console | json | memory — `memory` is the one tests assert against
LOG_FORMAT=console

# ── Storage ────────────────────────────────────────── L2 `postgres` ──
# memory | postgres
STORAGE=memory

# ── Events ───────────────────────────────────────────── L2 `events` ──
# memory | outbox — `outbox` requires STORAGE=postgres, since the outbox row is
# written in the same transaction as the data it announces
EVENTS_PROVIDER=memory

# ── Mail ─────────────────────────────────────────────── L2 `mailer` ──
# memory | smtp
MAIL_PROVIDER=memory

# ── Feature flags ─────────────────────────────────────── L3 `flags` ──
# static | file | postgres — unknown keys are off, whichever is chosen
FLAGS_PROVIDER=static

# ── Tenancy ──────────────────────────────────────────── L3 `tenant` ──
# single | multi — single mode is byte-identical to no tenancy, and fails closed
TENANT_MODE=single

# ── Telemetry ────────────────────────────────────── L1 `telemetry` ──
# none | otlp
TELEMETRY_TRACES=none
# none | prometheus
TELEMETRY_METRICS=none

# ── Rung 2 — the switch from memory to real ───────────────────────────
#
# Uncomment as each service joins `docker-compose.yml`. Every number below is
# `../PORTS.md` base + offset — this repo's base is 15420, its block is
# 15420-15439 — and every one is overridable: PG_PORT=25420 make db-up.
#
# +0  postgres           15420
# +1  redis              15421   (deferred: `cache` has a trigger)
# +2  mailpit smtp       15422
# +3  mailpit ui         15423
# +4  otlp http          15424
# +5  otlp grpc          15425
# +6  jaeger ui          15426
# +7  prometheus         15427
# +8  minio api          15428   (deferred: `blob` has a trigger)
# +9  minio console      15429
# +10 app                15430
# +11 app #2             15431   (a second instance, to prove the fleet-wide lock)
#
# STORAGE=postgres
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://app:app@localhost:15420/app?sslmode=disable
#
# EVENTS_PROVIDER=outbox
#
# MAIL_PROVIDER=smtp
# SMTP_HOST=localhost
# SMTP_PORT=15422
# SMTP_USERNAME=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
#
# TELEMETRY_TRACES=otlp
# TELEMETRY_METRICS=prometheus
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:15424

# ── Secret references ───────────────────────────────── L1 `secrets` ──
#
# ANY variable above may hold a reference instead of a literal. It is resolved
# before configuration is parsed, so nothing downstream can tell the difference
# — and a mounted Kubernetes secret needs no new code:
#
#   SMTP_PASSWORD=file:///run/secrets/smtp#password
#   SMTP_PASSWORD=env://SMTP_PASSWORD_REAL
